Dear Ms Payne,

Further to our telephone call, I attach a draft Defence in the claim brought =
by Jessica Payne against Anna Edwards (Claim No. N1EM5893).

I can confirm that the court (County Court at Cambridge) has listed the heari=
ng for 02/07/2024. Please confirm that you are able to attend.

Thank you for sending the documents. On a first review the case is well docum=
ented, although a few exhibits are still missing.

The draft is attached in Word format with tracked changes. Please send me you=
r comments by 11/12/2023, as the deadline for filing the response is fixed by=
 the court rules and cannot be extended without an application.

What we still need from you: confirmation of Jessica Payne's address (163 Lon=
don Lane, Bradford BD1 6LT), a copy of the payment slip for the deposit to ou=
r client account, and scans of your correspondence for the last two years.

The deposit towards court fees of =C2=A32,599.00 should reach our account GB3=
4MONZ04448223754317 no later than the day before the hearing.

Our witness, Gloria Parker, has been told that the court may require attendan=
ce; if her contact details (tel. 07700 900943) change, please let us know.

On strategy, I suggest we first seek the dismissal of the claim and, in the a=
lternative, ask the court to allow payment by instalments under CPR Part 40.

Please call me on 0161 496 0688 or write to adams.timothy@example.org if you =
have any questions.

I am copying my colleague Sandra Lee so that she can follow the file while I =
am out of the office.

Kind regards,

